@meta
id: 19-05
title: Every hit, one command
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: cdo
par: 85
minutes: 6
vscode: Replace All in Files
vimrc: set nohidden
open: README.md

@brief
`PaymentService.sendRefund` is becoming `issueRefund`. The definition,
every caller, every mock, every assertion: six lines across four files.
Chapter 14 gave you `:%s` for a whole file. This is the same thing for a
whole tree.

`:cdo` runs a command once for every entry in the quickfix list, with
the cursor on that entry. `:cdo s/sendRefund/issueRefund/g` is therefore
a substitute on each hit line, in whichever file it lives.

The part people forget is `| update`. The entries are in different
files, and vim will not leave a modified buffer behind while `hidden`
is off, which it is for this lesson, as it is in vim by default. Without
the `| update`, `:cdo` changes the first file, tries to move to the
second, and stops with E37. With it, each buffer is written before
`:cdo` moves on. It is `update` rather than `w` because `update` writes
only if something changed.

The README mentions the old name and stays: `**/*.ts` never opened it.

@keys
| `:cdo cmd` | run `cmd` on every quickfix entry |
| `:cdo s/old/new/g \| update` | the everyday form: substitute on the hit line, write, next |
| `:update` | write, but only if the buffer changed |

@hints
Fill the list first: `:vimgrep /sendRefund/ **/*.ts`. Six entries.
--
`:cdo s/sendRefund/issueRefund/g | update`. One line. Watch the
messages as it runs.
--
Everything is written by the time `:cdo` returns, so `:q` is enough to
leave.

@solution
    :vimgrep /sendRefund/ **/*.ts<Enter>  :cdo s/sendRefund/issueRefund/g | update<Enter>  :q<Enter>

Two commands. VS Code's Replace All in Files is one, and it is a fair
question why vim splits it. The answer is the list in between. After the
`:vimgrep` you can `:copen` and read what is about to change, and you
can decide not to change some of it, which the next two lessons are
about. Replace All shows a preview too; the difference is that vim's
preview is a list you can navigate, edit from, narrow by searching
again, and come back to later.

`| update` is the habit. Forgetting it does not corrupt anything; it
stops early with E37 and leaves you to run the `:cdo` again from where
it stopped, or to `:wa` if `hidden` happens to be on. Type it every time
and neither happens.

The `s` inside `:cdo` has no range, so it runs on the current line only,
which is the hit line. That is what you want: the list already knows
which lines matter, and `%s` here would be doing the search twice.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`.

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  placedAt: Date;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.issueRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).sendRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.sendRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
